                <pb facs="0421" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg333"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Lord Stanley of Preston.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Newport</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1892-09-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 9,
                    1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to your excellency’s
                    dispatch No. 49 of the 25th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose a copy of a note
                    which I have received from Mr. Foster in which he repeats that the President
                    cannot issue his proclamation until he is advised that the Canadian wrecking act
                    can be construed to apply to the Welland Canal.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Michael H.
                    Herbert.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
